---
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: LLVM

IndentWidth: 4
ContinuationIndentWidth: 4
TabWidth: 4
UseTab: Never

ColumnLimit: 120

# Allman - "Braces-Stand-Alone" in NASA SEL-94-003 7.1.2. See docs/CODE-STYLE.md.
# Previously Allman for functions only, K&R for control statements.
BreakBeforeBraces: Allman

# Bodies are always braced (CODE-STYLE.md, deviation from SEL-94-003 7.2.1).
#
# InsertBraces is what actually *adds* a missing brace; the AllowShort* keys
# below only stop clang-format collapsing an existing body back onto one line.
# Both are needed: without InsertBraces a brace-less `if (x) return;` is left
# exactly as written, which is the construct this project bans outright.
InsertBraces: true
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: None
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: Never
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: false
AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: Never
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: false

IndentCaseLabels: false

SortIncludes: Never
